---
const rows = [
  {
    what: "Map",
    goaccess: "Country table; a globe in the HTML report, not live",
    grafana: "Worldmap panel, if you ship a GeoIP pipeline yourself",
    us: ["Live map", " with routes, globe, heatmap, per-site homes"],
  },
  {
    what: "Setup",
    goaccess: "One binary, one log format string",
    grafana: "Promtail or Telegraf, a GeoIP processor, a dashboard JSON",
    us: ["Compose file", " with the database included; GeoLite2 downloads itself"],
  },
  {
    what: "History",
    goaccess: "Re-parses the file each run",
    grafana: "Whatever retention you configured",
    us: ["180 days raw", " by default, aggregates for long ranges, batch import for archives"],
  },
  {
    what: "Per-IP view",
    goaccess: "Top hosts list",
    grafana: "Build it",
    us: ["IP inspector", " with scanner tells and CrowdSec status"],
  },
  {
    what: "CrowdSec",
    goaccess: "No",
    grafana: "Dashboards only",
    us: ["Ban and unban", " from the map and tables; live decision badges"],
  },
  {
    what: "Several proxies",
    goaccess: "One file at a time",
    grafana: "Yes, that is what it is for",
    us: ["Agents", " next to each log, one database, one map"],
  },
];
---

<section class="compare" id="compare">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="section-title">Why not the tools you already have?</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      You can get a country breakdown out of GoAccess, and a world map out of Grafana with enough plumbing. This is
      what changes.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th></th><th>GoAccess</th><th>Grafana + Loki / Influx</th><th>GeoMetrikks</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{r.what}</td>
              <td>{r.goaccess}</td>
              <td>{r.grafana}</td>
              <td>
                <b>{r.us[0]}</b>
                {r.us[1]}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .compare {
    padding: 100px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .section-title {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }
  .sub {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0 0 36px;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 14px 16px 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  th {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  td:first-child {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
    width: 22%;
  }
  td {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
  }
  td b {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .compare {
      padding: 64px 0;
    }
    table {
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    th:nth-child(2),
    td:nth-child(2) {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
